NOTICE — scope of this license

The MIT license above covers the LeapSinger **source code** only. It does NOT
cover the following, which have their own separate terms. `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`
gives the details for each.

  - `preprocess/algorithms/base.py` and `preprocess/algorithms/rmvpe.py`. Both
    were taken verbatim from pitch-benchmark
    (https://github.com/lars76/pitch-benchmark), MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Lars
    Nieradzik, whose notice is in `LICENSES/pitch-benchmark-MIT.txt` and must be
    kept when redistributing. `base.py` is MIT like the rest of this repository.

    `rmvpe.py` is **not**: the RMVPE model inside it
    (https://github.com/Dream-High/RMVPE) is Apache-2.0 upstream, so that one
    file is distributed under the **Apache License, Version 2.0**, whose full
    text is in `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`. Its `to_local_average_cents()`
    originates in CREPE (https://github.com/marl/crepe), whose MIT notice —
    Copyright (c) 2018 Jong Wook Kim — is in `LICENSES/crepe-MIT.txt`.
    The RMVPE weights (`rmvpe.pt`) are downloaded at run time and are not
    distributed with this repository.

  - The demo and sample audio (`demo/audio/*_gt.ogg`,
    `notebooks/sample_data/*.wav`). These are excerpts of real recordings from
    the singing databases named below, not synthesis output, and stay governed by
    each database's terms of use.

  - The bundled neural vocoder ONNX files (`checkpoints/nhv_v3_2.onnx`,
    `checkpoints/nhv_v3_2x.onnx`). These come from the NHVSing project
    (https://github.com/wavtechyukky/NHVSing/) and are governed by its license.

  - The trained acoustic-model checkpoints distributed via GitHub Releases, and
    the singing-voice databases used to train them (Oniku Kurumi, Natsume Yuuri,
    Namine Ritsu). These are governed by each database's own terms of use — see
    `CREDITS.txt` bundled with the model release. In particular, credit and,
    for some databases, the bundled terms of use must be kept when redistributing.
